          {
            "id": "1001",
            "author_id": "1",
            "created_at": "2026-11-23T14:25:00.000Z",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "AI agents look fine in the demo and then fall over in operations. The workflow they were given was the happy path. Production is the exceptions.",
            "public_metrics": {"like_count": 40, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 10, "quote_count": 3, "impression_count": 12000}
          },
          {
            "id": "1002",
            "author_id": "2",
            "created_at": "2026-11-23T13:00:00.000Z",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "The useful question about AI at work is not whether the model can do the task once. It is whether the person still checks every row before the process can move.",
            "public_metrics": {"like_count": 30, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 4, "quote_count": 1, "impression_count": 8000}
          },
          {
            "id": "1003",
            "author_id": "3",
            "created_at": "2026-11-23T12:00:00.000Z",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "B2B buyers do not purchase a category. They purchase relief from a process that already has a budget. GTM teams forget that when they sell AI.",
            "public_metrics": {"like_count": 55, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 9, "quote_count": 2, "impression_count": 20000}
          },
          {
            "id": "1004",
            "author_id": "4",
            "created_at": "2026-11-23T09:40:00.000Z",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "SaaS implementation fails when the new workflow sits beside the old one. Nothing is removed, so cycle time does not move.",
            "public_metrics": {"like_count": 18, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "impression_count": 4000}
          },
          {
            "id": "1005",
            "author_id": "5",
            "created_at": "2026-11-23T13:30:00.000Z",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "Positioning is about the budget they already have. For many ops teams that budget is not AI. It is the cost of the process.",
            "public_metrics": {"like_count": 22, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 3, "quote_count": 1, "impression_count": 5000}
          },
          {
            "id": "1006",
            "author_id": "6",
            "created_at": "2026-11-23T14:05:00.000Z",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "Tools are not the workflow. If you want automation to stick, start from the queue: who touches the file, and which step they quietly do twice.",
            "public_metrics": {"like_count": 36, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 5, "quote_count": 1, "impression_count": 15000}
          },
          {
            "id": "1008",
            "author_id": "1",
            "created_at": "2026-11-23T14:10:00.000Z",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "You should not turn off the old workflow on day one of an automation pilot. Run the new one in the shadow and compare.",
            "public_metrics": {"like_count": 20, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 4, "quote_count": 1, "impression_count": 6000}
          },
          {
            "id": "1009",
            "author_id": "8",
            "created_at": "2026-11-23T14:40:00.000Z",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "AI agents will rebuild the back office. The workflow software of the last twenty years is done.",
            "public_metrics": {"like_count": 8000, "reply_count": 500, "retweet_count": 1200, "quote_count": 200, "impression_count": 2000000}
          },
          {
            "id": "1010",
            "author_id": "9",
            "created_at": "2026-11-23T14:30:00.000Z",
            "lang": "en",
            "text": "Back office automation is the whole game for insurance operations.",
            "public_metrics": {"like_count": 4, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "impression_count": 200}
          },
          {
            "id": "1011",
